Description: Provides a label-informed reference-learning and bias-correction
    method for microbiome sequencing data. It iteratively screens and refines
    a candidate reference set to reduce contamination by differentially
    abundant taxa, then uses the selected reference taxa to estimate relative
    sampling depths across samples. Correcting the sample-specific scaling of
    observed read counts supports recovery of taxon-specific fold changes on
    the absolute-abundance scale and integration with downstream differential
    abundance analysis frameworks.
